400           * Node id fix up. Actual hardware supports up to 4 nodes. But with
   401           * more than 32 cores, we may end up with more than 4 nodes.
   402           * Node id is a combination of socket id and node id. Only requirement
   403           * here is that this number should be unique accross the system.
   404           * Shift the socket id to accommodate more nodes. We dont expect both
   405           * socket id and node id to be big number at the same time. This is not
   406           * an ideal config but we need to to support it. Max nodes we can have
   407           * is 32 (255/8) with 8 cores per node and 255 max cores. We only need
   408           * 5 bits for nodes. Find the left most set bit to represent the total
   409           * number of nodes. find_last_bit returns last set bit(0 based). Left
   410           * shift(+1) the socket id to represent all the nodes.
   411           */
   412          nodes -= 1;
   413          shift = find_last_bit(&nodes, 8);
   414          *ecx = (nodes << 8) | (topo_ids.pkg_id << (shift + 1)) |
   415                 topo_ids.node_id;
   416      }
   417      *edx = 0;
